Attribution / origin
----------------------------------------------------------------------
This project originally began as a fork of Facebook AI Research's reference
implementation of Poincaré embeddings
(https://github.com/facebookresearch/poincare-embeddings), which implements the
method of:

    Nickel, M. & Kiela, D. (2017). "Poincaré Embeddings for Learning
    Hierarchical Representations." Advances in Neural Information Processing
    Systems 30 (NeurIPS 2017). arXiv:1705.08039.

That reference code was open-sourced by Facebook Research in 2018 under the
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 (CC BY-NC 4.0) license. Since the
fork, the codebase has been entirely reimplemented for biological taxonomy: the
training driver, transitive-closure/dataset builders, evaluation suite, CLI,
optimizer, and figures are original work, and no source code from the original
implementation remains in this repository. The Riemannian gradient rescaling in
src/taxembed/optim/riemannian.py is a clean-room reimplementation of the
Poincaré-ball conformal-factor formula described by Nickel & Kiela (2017),
copying no original source text.

We gratefully acknowledge Nickel & Kiela for the original method.
